//
// qwen3_0_6b profiling: compile then profile on NPU2, capturing TTFT + decode
// throughput into qwen3_0_6b.perf.json via bench/extract_perf.py. Perf is best-effort
// (a model that does not print a metric yields null); this test gates only that
// profiling ran end to end. Collected by the CI target
// check-programming-examples-llms-profile. Correctness is gated separately by
// run_npu2_verify.lit.
//
// `[2026-08-26]` PRECISION (doc 56 H2b, queue item 24): this profiles the
// production DEFAULT, which is now the int4 `w4_decode` decode path
// (`QWEN3_W4_DECODE` defaults to 1). The perf.json this emits is therefore the
// int4 decode number from that date on; `QWEN3_W4_DECODE=0` profiles the bf16
// A/B arm. The precision is deliberately NOT pinned here: this test's job is to
// report what production does, and run_npu2_verify.lit is where both
// precisions are pinned and gated.
//
// `clean-build`, NOT `clean`: `make clean` also deletes
// `$(srcdir)/../verify/reports/`, a source-tree path not scoped to this test's
// cwd (item 20 recorded the same hazard on the llama int4 bfp16 lit). This test
// only needs its own build tree gone.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, hf_token, hfweights_qwen_qwen3_0_6b
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_profile
// RUN: cd test_peano_profile
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean-build
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile profile PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR N_TOKENS=128 PROMPT="What is the capital of France?" | tee profile.txt
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/extract_perf.py profile.txt --model qwen3_0_6b > qwen3_0_6b.perf.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < qwen3_0_6b.perf.json
// CHECK: "model": "qwen3_0_6b"
